==============================================================================
fib TG 2.4.3 / R65 — parameter study
==============================================================================
Clause numbers below — 6.1, 6.2.2, 6.2.3, 3.2.7(2), Table 3.1 — refer to DIN EN 1992-1-1:2011-01, i.e. EN 1992-1-1:2004 + AC:2010, the edition in this repository as DINEN1992-1-1.pdf. Investigation 4 is the exception and says so where it happens: it uses EN 1992-1-1:2023, which renumbers the standard, so clause references are not comparable across that boundary.

==============================================================================
1. Q5 — mean level vs the experiment, beam as built (with stirrups)
==============================================================================
Same EC2 equations, gamma_M = 1.0, measured mean strengths, actions unfactored. This separates model bias from safety margin.

steel branch                  M_R [kNm]   P [kN]  R_exp/R_calc
horizontal (EC2 3.2.7(2)b )       234.0    224.8         1.153
inclined (EC2 3.2.7(2)a )         252.5    243.2         1.066

measured R_exp = 259.2 kN
The residual gap is strain hardening, which the horizontal branch discards:this beam is very under-reinforced and the steel is highly ductile.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.1  Which mode governs at mean level
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The comparison above is a bending comparison, which is only meaningful if the specimen could not have failed in shear first.

bending (EC2 6.1)                                        P =   224.8 kN
with stirrups (EC2 6.2.3)    theta = 25.63 deg  V_R  =  577.8 kN   P =   568.4 kN
without stirrups (EC2 6.2.2  )                    V_R,c=  108.4 kN   P =    99.1 kN  (116.3 kN with the a_v < 2d allowance)

as built, bending governs by 2.5x — the Q5 comparison is a flexural one, confirmed.
without stirrups the beam would have failed in shear at roughly 99-116 kN, far below R_exp = 259.2 kN
— a preview of why Q7 falls so far below Q6 (investigation 3).

CAVEAT the mean computation without stirrups after EC2 6.2.2 is a hybrid: C_Rd,c = 0.18/gamma_C keeps the characteristic-level constant 0.18 at gamma_C = 1, and nu = 0.6(1-f_ck/250)in the mean computation with stirrups after EC2 6.2.3 is a strut effectiveness factor calibrated on f_ck, not a strength. Neither is a true R(x_m). Immaterial at this margin.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.2  Sensitivity to the assumed eps_uk, inclined branch after EC2 3.2.7(2)a 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
eps_uk is never reached by this section, so it does not change the horizontal branch at all. It does set the slope of the inclined branch: E_h = (f_td - f_yd)/(eps_ud - eps_yd) with eps_ud = 0.9 eps_uk.

  eps_uk   M horiz [kNm]   M incl [kNm]  P incl [kN]  R_exp/R_calc
   0.050           234.0          267.9        258.7         1.002
   0.075           234.0          257.9        248.6         1.042
   0.100           234.0          252.5        243.2         1.066  <- params.yaml
   0.150           234.0          246.7        237.5         1.091
   0.231           234.0          242.5        233.3         1.111

0.231 would be A_10 = 23.1 %, the elongation after fracture — NOT eps_uk. The qualitative conclusion holds across the range; the specific ratio does not, so it should be quoted as a range, not as a single number.

