2. Q6 — maximum design value of P, beam as built (with stirrups)
==============================================================================
level = design   branch = elasticperfectlyplastic   case = with_stirrups
  materials      f_ck =   8.71 MPa   f_cd =  5.807 MPa   f_yk =  364.5 MPa   f_yd =  317.0 MPa
  self weight    g_k  = 4.6875 kN/m   M_g = 9.223 kNm   V_g = 9.375 kN   (gamma_G = 1.35)
  bending after EC2 6.1            M_R  =   171.41 kNm  ->  P =   159.0 kN
  shear after EC2 6.2.3          V_R  =   262.16 kN   ->  P =   249.5 kN   (theta = 39.84 deg, cot = 1.199, V_R,s = 262.6, V_R,max = 262.2 kN)
  ==>  P = 159.0 kN   (bending governs)
       P_k = P / 1.5 = 106.0 kN

bending governs by 1.6x over the shear verification (EC2 6.2.3), so the answer to Q6 is set by bending verification (EC2 6.1) alone. The target p_f = 1e-6 that Q6 names is the subject of investigation 4.

